Confirm one external import instead of every handle type — PUNKTFUNK LOCAL PATCH.

Not upstream. `pyrowave_device_confirm_interop_support` passes only when the device imports
all five Win32 memory handle types with STORAGE|SAMPLED usage, plus OPAQUE_WIN32 binary and
timeline semaphores and a D3D12 fence. The Windows host imports D3D11 textures with
SAMPLED|TRANSFER usage and one D3D12 fence, so a GPU lacking any unused type was refused.

WHAT IT DOES. Adds `pyrowave_device_confirm_image_import_support` (one handle type, format
and usage) and `pyrowave_device_confirm_semaphore_import_support` (one handle type, asked
without a type chain as upstream asks a D3D12 fence). Upstream's check is unchanged.

